# Git branches, commits, and PR lifecycle

Do not use Cursor’s default `cursor/` branch prefix unless the user explicitly asks for it.

## Branches

- Track work: `track-<nnn>-<kebab-slug>` (example: `track-121-frontend-toolchain`)
- Otherwise: `<type>/<kebab-slug>` where type is `fix`, `feat`, `docs`, `chore`, or `ci` (example: `fix/ragamalika-parser-and-section-matching`)
- Reuse the current branch when it already matches the work
- Do not commit directly on `main` unless the user explicitly asks

## Commits

Follow `.agents/skills/commit-policy/SKILL.md`. Do not commit until the user asks.

```text
<TRACK-ID>: <short summary>

Ref: application_documentation/<path>.md

- <bullet>
```

Omit `TRACK-ID` only when no conductor track exists. Every commit needs exactly one `Ref:` line pointing at an existing file under `application_documentation/` (prefer `application_documentation/10-implementations/`).

Never stage `.env`, `config/local.env`, `config/development.env`, credentials, or secrets. Never use `git add .` or `git commit -a`.

## Push & Pull Request

1. Push branch: `git push -u origin HEAD` (never force-push, never skip hooks).
2. Create or reuse PR: `gh pr create --base main --head $(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD) --title "<TRACK-ID>: <summary>" --body "..."`
3. Watch CI checks until they finish: `gh pr checks --watch`
4. Never merge while any check is pending or failing. Fix failures on the branch and re-watch.

## Merge & Local Sync

1. Merge into remote `main`: `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch` (never use `--admin` to bypass protection).
2. Sync local with remote `main`:
   ```bash
   git fetch origin --prune
   git checkout main
   git pull --ff-only origin main
   ```

## Stale Branch Cleanup

Stale branches are those already merged into `origin/main` or whose upstream is gone (`[gone]`).
- Never delete `main`. Never delete an unmerged branch. Use safe delete (`git branch -d`).
- Delete merged local branch: `git branch -d <branch-name>`
- Delete merged remote branch if not deleted by PR merge: `git push origin --delete <branch-name>`
- Delete a local branch whose upstream is gone only when `git branch -d` accepts it. Leave unmerged branches in place:
  ```bash
  git branch -vv | awk '/: gone]/ {print $1}' | while read -r b; do [ -n "$b" ] && git branch -d "$b"; done
  ```
